# Fork isolation (upstream merge safety)

This repo is a **fork** of `CodeWithCJ/SparkyFitness`. Custom work must stay easy to rebase/merge when upstream updates.

## Branch roles

- `main` — mirror upstream; do not land fork-only features here
- `deploy` — Coolify production branch
- `feature/*` — fork features (e.g. AI meal log); merge into `deploy`, not upstream PRs unless asked

## Isolation rules for new work

- Prefer **new files** (routes, services, pages, hooks, schemas, prompts, tests) over rewriting upstream modules
- Touch existing upstream files only with **thin hooks**: one import, one button, one `app.use`, one prop — never large refactors inside shared upstream code
- Do **not** create a parallel `custom/` tree unless the user asks; keep domain files in normal package layout, but keep them additive
- Extract shared helpers on the second duplication; put reusable cascade/logic in dedicated services so chat + meal-log + food-draft share one path
- Avoid drive-by renames, formatting sweeps, or “cleanup” of untouched upstream files — those fight merges
- Migrations / RLS / shared Zod: follow package checklists; still prefer additive schema changes

## When unsure

Prefer: new endpoint + new UI dialog + 3-line mount in an existing file  
Over: editing a large upstream service “in place” to bolt on behavior

## Docs

Update `docs/content/1.install/12.fork-ai-meal-log.md` (or a sibling fork note) when adding Coolify/ops-facing fork features.
